enamelpin-by-suricrasiaonline for Debian
----------------------------------------

* The packaged executable is the "unpacked" version described in README.txt:
  the 4k version is compressed with smol and vondehi, which need a hand-tuned
  x86-64 toolchain.
* The x86-64 _start entry point and raw syscalls of the 4k version are
  replaced by a standard main() and _exit() (02_portable-entry-point.patch),
  so the demo is also built for i386, armhf and arm64.
* The shader is minified at build time with the system shader_minifier.exe
  (shader-minifier package) instead of the copy shipped upstream.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>, reviewed by Nicolas HOUDELOT.

